body:
Review under #66: keep this research evidence, but correct the PR headline before presenting the proposed policy as fully detecting declared harms. The detailed report §10.4.1 is explicit:

- proposed two blocking checks (delta-B + shift): holdout253/270;
- adding scale<=0.01: holdout270/270;
- proposal §10.4 labels scale as warning/nonblocking.

Therefore270/270 is not the measured sensitivity of the proposed two-check blocking policy. Also retain delta-B's incoherent-damage blind spot and the declared harm-class distinction; an attributed harmless scale change and a detector gain defect are not automatically interchangeable.

Current stabilization uses the separate explicit backend profile in #75: preserves legacy exact/relaxed results; retains relativeRMSE as a named nonblocking diagnostic while keeping existing absolute-image/max-pixel/trajectory/static-metadata checks and requiring complete finite products +process evidence. This is not adoption of §10's proposed replacement gate or a scientific equivalence claim. #73 tracks independent-collection validation.
